{"title":"1994 OIM Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is said to be \"<i>sensible</i>\" if there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08ebe246a7285dbcc1fb4025bae9886312573d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;r&lt;n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, such that the representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has all its digits equal. For example, 62 and 15 are \"<i>sensible</i>\", since 62 is 222 in base 5 and 15 is 33 in base 4.\n</p><p>Prove that 1993 is NOT \"<i>sensible</i>\" but 1994 is.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lemma:\nEvery number that can be expressed as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c2af04ade2533d704845b75e2a89892441e1265.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b \\cdot \\frac{r^d-1}{r-1} , b &lt; r\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"39\" />\nIs a \"<i>sensible</i>\" number as it can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1baf81bce1b8aa64c7c2bc67304652c7e19c03f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\cdots b _ r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, where there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41ab427d350cd5559a110faf52cae7c999b9fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b’s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Part <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c48f75b5eb43530c84af32fbcfbd6dda062921a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> Let us prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45fabf5c3fa51caa9ab513719e62d0bb8f95157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1993$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be expressed as such.\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45fabf5c3fa51caa9ab513719e62d0bb8f95157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1993$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a prime, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> as it cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45fabf5c3fa51caa9ab513719e62d0bb8f95157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1993$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> or else <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/7000a4df7498208edbd9cbd4e8303d1958b219d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />.\nTherefore, we need to prove that there does not exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954606e392af6e7ad0e7d896467fe777640016a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d,r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab4360189286f6c91b9aa131d871d63abcefb1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{r^d-1}{r-1} =1993\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"39\" />\nAssume on the contrary, there exists such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954606e392af6e7ad0e7d896467fe777640016a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d,r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />. Then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1cec2c4e4ec21581cfa40e35202c548c411d5661.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^d - 1 = 1993r - 1993 \\implies r^d = 1993r - 1992\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"16\" />\nNotice that taking mod<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/dea9ff909f0f609d7c6163285c922cc93ff6cfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad594d7b1bd37df24b61e9ab4896c4b7bb493d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\mid 1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />. \nNotice plugging in some small values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542bf09223409b3975968a1b2d3b231038325676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 2,3,4,6,8,12,24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"17\" />, they don’t work\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b3392726a6bb850c84c12ba5425f9a6cde0568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1992 \\cdot 2 - 1992 = 1994 \\neq 2^d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"21\" />\nAnd similarly.\nSo the next smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1ad4a48099624f3bbfc16590f9be2d29351d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$83$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8eb4576f786ea6425b92fa53138632210704232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> because \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d11750604de2f30bb731edba14d7812866b1c3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{when} \\hspace{0.2cm} r \\geq 45, r^3 &gt; 1993r -1992\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2471a708cb8167c372f2215758379284f3bf332d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> grows faster than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec4b4343639012562c8b3071e8e2b405c48eb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1992r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328c29bfd644f207e354321e2397448cdab49e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; \\sqrt{1992} \\implies r \\geq 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"187\" height=\"22\" /> and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61d9398e34f1d14ab65a39c28c123a9ebfc0d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 45, 45^3 = 91125 &gt; 87693 = 1993 \\cdot 45 - 1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3173fa662c519084af54a3128ce7b3ecb7ee08e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a4e41e9d7b45ad6a4d06a9c38abce8676cc1d30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/305031a955d678ce38c314aae5020d8cd0921db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1992(r-1) = 0 \\implies r = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" />, which is not true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9066f25538d897b813554873248c9b81a6646de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe71c3211e3d450a050481828e32454c7a466e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a90f7ac15692f9fd7596d0d87f9a509df6cabd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)(r-1992) = 0 \\implies r = 1,1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"307\" height=\"20\" />, which is not true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778b1e205fc17efcca06461a390ea18b61048219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;r&lt;1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\nSo there is no solution.\n</p><p>Part <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff1be62d9bb7a4e1e12b6ecef0d2f43c133e9c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> Let us show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b6fb7a1d8b2bd77671950bb223396c2c43af6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1994$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is sensible.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e872522f160bc7c459b5e97a2e101b1818913b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1994 = 2 \\cdot 997 = 2\\cdot (996 + 1) = 22_{996}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Comment: any composite number other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime is sensible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47fa28ca4439471cfe91c2fbe32d4aad988ea5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot r = n \\cdot (1 + (r-1)) = nn_{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" />\nE.g <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246dc03950d857f99a70a6f55f2fcbd26c58c185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69 = 3\\cdot 23 = 33_{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n~Archieguan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe9.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe9.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017025715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 233/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8142/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26089:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017025715 and revision id 230377. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}